  "description": "There’s one in every family. That one that feels excluded from the bunch. If you’re down with that attitude because you like to go your own way, then we’d like to introduce you to the rowdiest member of the RSD family – the MiddleChild.\n\nSome of our bikes are great at getting the job done – real authorities. The 29/27.5+ MiddleChild gets it done, but the only thing on the agenda is playtime. Every detail on this premium-quality handmade steel frame screams “skip work and let’s party!”\n\ndouble-butted, heat-treated 4130 Chromoly steel tubing\n\ndouble-butted, heat-treated 4130 Chromoly steel tubing\n\nfull CNC-machined custom yoke that’ll take 2.8″ tires (or up to 2.6″ x 29)\n\nfull CNC-machined custom yoke that’ll take 2.8″ tires (or up to 2.6″ x 29)\n\n64.5 degree head tube and the V3 sports a brand new 75 degree seat tube angle paired with 140mm fork, which in turn has also increased the Reach by approx. 10mm across all sizes – that aggressive geometry for both climbing and sending choice descent lines\n\n64.5 degree head tube and the V3 sports a brand new 75 degree seat tube angle paired with 140mm fork, which in turn has also increased the Reach by approx. 10mm across all sizes – that aggressive geometry for both climbing and sending choice descent lines\n\nboost spacing and short chainstays (adjustable from 415mm – 430mm) for super stability and loads of confidence in the rough stuff\n\nboost spacing and short chainstays (adjustable from 415mm – 430mm) for super stability and loads of confidence in the rough stuff\n\nThe new V2 has a shorter and straighter seat tube on all sizes to allow for an even longer dropper post\n\nThe new V2 has a shorter and straighter seat tube on all sizes to allow for an even longer dropper post\n\nChoose from either Duroc 40 27.5+ wheels with Maxxis Minion DHF & DHR II 2.8 tires or Duroc 35 29in wheels with Maxxis Minion DHF 2.5 Front and Aggressor 2.5 Rear\n\nChoose from either Duroc 40 27.5+ wheels with Maxxis Minion DHF & DHR II 2.8 tires or Duroc 35 29in wheels with Maxxis Minion DHF 2.5 Front and Aggressor 2.5 Rear\n\nThe MiddleChild is a purely new-school ‘Enduro’ hardtail…\n\n…that will never get left behind.",
